{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:18:44.697110Z","id":"ec23bc9083f7bbe07cc553ab5f0414c82930f82a1a5689432a1e6c8b9e919ab0","body":{"detail":"target/gates.log of the toolpath-audit worktree at bf1180d: AssertionError expected length 2 but got 4 at clax.test.ts:800. Not reproduced in 32 runs of the tier 5 tests under 8-way parallel load, nor in 5 runs of the Pi lane alone and 5 under 20 busy processes. trackPolls now records each poll's tier and client and the counts assert on pollsSeen(polls), so the next failure names the extra polls; the fake daemon now answers tool-call reports, so the case no longer waits 3 s at shutdown (that wait came after the failing assertion and is not the cause).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":760},"end":{"line":808},"content_hash":"23af039100f651dd8f641ac591f9f6101ff35dcdcbb2e0ab6f25c430e61d01ac"},"suggested_fix":"On the next failure, read which tier and client made the extra polls from the assertion's diff.","summary":"Unexplained flake: 'tier 5 holds… (parked 2000 ms)' saw 4 inject polls instead of 2 in the quality gate run of bf1180d","tags":["review","tests","flaky","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
