{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.125475Z","id":"38058e03dff995d89528404ef61a9607f956ccd52ef88f355e08616ed47b3318","body":{"detail":"Seen once on 2026-10-13 in a full vitest run of plugins/pi while a cargo build ran beside it (expect.poll(() => polls.length).toBe(1) received 7 within its 10 s). Alone, and in the next two full runs, it passed. trackPolls counts every DaemonClient's inject polls, so a poll of another loop, or a quick series of early returns paced by injectRetryMs (250 ms), would both count; which one this was is not known. Compare 6fab3d3d, a count flake in another tier 5 test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1198},"end":{"line":1231},"content_hash":"f569dab282bd8b4473edd666b40890f77340398bd460c8470e07f8ecb45763df"},"summary":"Unexplained flake: 'the injection loop never starts a stopped daemon, and resumes when one is back' saw 7 inject polls where it waits for 1","supersedes":"9bab01321405af8ab4a5e8a9d9d4b0fdc7679af7c60714b3c017cf47098ebb8c","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/remote.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.139322Z","id":"ef50a67e38c5cbc30ea9698bbe5a2e7e453c9aefbf0aa93efb539aec549cd260","body":{"detail":"`ahead` is computed once (line 321); learnOffset (plugins/pi/src/remote.ts:183) takes round(Date) - floor(now), so every second between computing `ahead` and the answer lowers the offset by one, and the Date header's whole seconds take up to one more. On a machine with a load average near 200 a vitest worker can stall that long.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":381},"end":{"line":398},"content_hash":"a680bdb4d36fac7242cc2ac83e70203561ed40f3b9ea7d47b7d987ae59ae035b"},"suggested_fix":"Let the fake daemon compute the Date when it answers (Date.now() + 100_000 inside the handler), or assert the offset within a wider bound.","summary":"The stale-request test asserts |offset - 100| <= 2, with the daemon's Date fixed before two servers start and the home is connected: a stall of about 1-2 s before the request is answered fails it","supersedes":"abaa6166bb98a421ccb69bf41c47a8f23861f42a12c7913e384fc42a1341d747","tags":["review","tests","flake","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:53:20.511724Z","id":"89bf32fccacbbd2e53a5f09624d25a17aa853bd92f5a2835b64634b5246500a1","body":{"detail":"The test emits an input with source \"extension\" and then one with source \"interactive\", and polls until signals.terminal_at is set. The interactive input alone sets it, so the test passes whether or not the extension input is recorded. The handler at plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1900:1906 sends POST /api/sessions/<sid>/terminal fire-and-forget, so no event marks that an extension input's request did not happen without a sleep. A check could stand on an observable: for example a fake daemon (plugins/pi/test/fake-api.ts) that records requests, emitting the extension input, then an awaited tool call on the same client, and asserting no POST .../terminal was seen.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1065},"end":{"line":1074},"content_hash":"68f092d1acfeb5773078b6f96350e6c6210feebba012208202acaa0f2b1d1939"},"suggested_fix":"Assert on the requests a fake daemon received, or expose the handler's request promise to tests.","summary":"The Pi input test does not prove an extension-sent message is ignored","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:03:15.462505Z","id":"98688aa4180da6a6238c761bc82923abf96d22a9a733a2073903f78ca3ed6dea","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c25eb5f3d","summary":"The test now spies on DaemonClient.prototype.noteTerminal (pass-through) and asserts no call after the extension input and one call after the interactive input; FakePi.emit awaits each handler and the handler calls noteTerminal before returning, so no sleep is needed. With the `event.source !== \"extension\"` guard in plugins/pi/src/clax.ts replaced by `true`, `bazelisk test //plugins/pi:test --test_arg=-t --test_arg=\"a prompt typed in Pi\"` failed: AssertionError: expected \"noteTerminal\" to not be called at all, but actually been called 1 times. With the guard restored, `bazelisk test //plugins/pi:test //plugins/pi:typecheck` passed (116/116 tests).","supersedes":"89bf32fccacbbd2e53a5f09624d25a17aa853bd92f5a2835b64634b5246500a1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.775447Z","id":"fd6291c3246c9526966354008147e3806043a9c7fc26c217a640d6e98818db31","body":{"detail":"target/gates.log of the toolpath-audit worktree at bf1180d: AssertionError expected length 2 but got 4 at clax.test.ts:800. Not reproduced in 32 runs of the tier 5 tests under 8-way parallel load, nor in 5 runs of the Pi lane alone and 5 under 20 busy processes. trackPolls now records each poll's tier and client and the counts assert on pollsSeen(polls), so the next failure names the extra polls; the fake daemon now answers tool-call reports, so the case no longer waits 3 s at shutdown (that wait came after the failing assertion and is not the cause).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":857},"end":{"line":905},"content_hash":"23af039100f651dd8f641ac591f9f6101ff35dcdcbb2e0ab6f25c430e61d01ac"},"suggested_fix":"On the next failure, read which tier and client made the extra polls from the assertion's diff.","summary":"Unexplained flake: 'tier 5 holds… (parked 2000 ms)' saw 4 inject polls instead of 2 in the quality gate run of bf1180d","supersedes":"a1eaa369b293738ff4d71bb581d0a6b66f91b5b6c25412561965391719ff3036","tags":["review","tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.797923Z","id":"9de4d1e72368d40f36a59d79261b64ca0365e99ec73173dc200f63d2c275aeb0","body":{"detail":"Seen once on 2026-10-13 in a full vitest run of plugins/pi while a cargo build ran beside it (expect.poll(() => polls.length).toBe(1) received 7 within its 10 s). Alone, and in the next two full runs, it passed. trackPolls counts every DaemonClient's inject polls, so a poll of another loop, or a quick series of early returns paced by injectRetryMs (250 ms), would both count; which one this was is not known. Compare 6fab3d3d, a count flake in another tier 5 test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1261},"end":{"line":1294},"content_hash":"f569dab282bd8b4473edd666b40890f77340398bd460c8470e07f8ecb45763df"},"summary":"Unexplained flake: 'the injection loop never starts a stopped daemon, and resumes when one is back' saw 7 inject polls where it waits for 1","supersedes":"38058e03dff995d89528404ef61a9607f956ccd52ef88f355e08616ed47b3318","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T14:01:01.408796Z","id":"7f062ba82d09be650df295f3d8275ca19a3c657cd685032ddd0027f214dec5ae","body":{"detail":"In a just check run with all lanes at once (2026-10-19, on the commits after 472e8c948), //plugins/pi:test failed: AssertionError: expected [ 'GET /healthz' ] to include 'POST /api/sessions' at plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts:453. The test passes startBudgetMs: 50 (line 449) and asserts the hung daemon saw the registration; under load the 50 ms budget runs out during the health check, before the extension reaches POST /api/sessions. just pi-test alone passed right after. A wall-clock budget in a test conflicts with AGENTS.md (load-tolerant tests, injected clocks for timing rules); an injected clock for the start budget, or asserting only that session_start returns, would remove it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":443},"end":{"line":457},"content_hash":"f4abfc2ba9a2d0d89833e1ae8d64aaca1c5b446d15088affc7ce14e2f0bc99b4"},"summary":"Load flake: 'gives up registering at session_start when its budget runs out while the daemon hangs' saw only GET /healthz within its 50 ms budget","tags":["flake","session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:33.491019Z","id":"f24c538fc227996a2a76c84ca4a959f36efa856be824e6bb13b28e3d998aa7f1","body":{"detail":"target/gates.log of the toolpath-audit worktree at bf1180d: AssertionError expected length 2 but got 4 at clax.test.ts:800. Not reproduced in 32 runs of the tier 5 tests under 8-way parallel load, nor in 5 runs of the Pi lane alone and 5 under 20 busy processes. trackPolls now records each poll's tier and client and the counts assert on pollsSeen(polls), so the next failure names the extra polls; the fake daemon now answers tool-call reports, so the case no longer waits 3 s at shutdown (that wait came after the failing assertion and is not the cause).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":996},"end":{"line":1044},"content_hash":"23af039100f651dd8f641ac591f9f6101ff35dcdcbb2e0ab6f25c430e61d01ac"},"suggested_fix":"On the next failure, read which tier and client made the extra polls from the assertion's diff.","summary":"Unexplained flake: 'tier 5 holds… (parked 2000 ms)' saw 4 inject polls instead of 2 in the quality gate run of bf1180d","supersedes":"fd6291c3246c9526966354008147e3806043a9c7fc26c217a640d6e98818db31","tags":["review","tests","flaky","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:33.593120Z","id":"6b375e2f714dfb738b47aa45a7004cb938508eae33298dd045c502effc570ab3","body":{"detail":"Seen once on 2026-10-13 in a full vitest run of plugins/pi while a cargo build ran beside it (expect.poll(() => polls.length).toBe(1) received 7 within its 10 s). Alone, and in the next two full runs, it passed. trackPolls counts every DaemonClient's inject polls, so a poll of another loop, or a quick series of early returns paced by injectRetryMs (250 ms), would both count; which one this was is not known. Compare 6fab3d3d, a count flake in another tier 5 test.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1430},"end":{"line":1463},"content_hash":"f569dab282bd8b4473edd666b40890f77340398bd460c8470e07f8ecb45763df"},"summary":"Unexplained flake: 'the injection loop never starts a stopped daemon, and resumes when one is back' saw 7 inject polls where it waits for 1","supersedes":"9de4d1e72368d40f36a59d79261b64ca0365e99ec73173dc200f63d2c275aeb0","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/remote.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:33.696525Z","id":"87c61ee74edaea3ea0d426283afdee1dd8d734d117faa082a65bb065ea9117d3","body":{"detail":"`ahead` is computed once (line 321); learnOffset (plugins/pi/src/remote.ts:183) takes round(Date) - floor(now), so every second between computing `ahead` and the answer lowers the offset by one, and the Date header's whole seconds take up to one more. On a machine with a load average near 200 a vitest worker can stall that long.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":454},"end":{"line":471},"content_hash":"a680bdb4d36fac7242cc2ac83e70203561ed40f3b9ea7d47b7d987ae59ae035b"},"suggested_fix":"Let the fake daemon compute the Date when it answers (Date.now() + 100_000 inside the handler), or assert the offset within a wider bound.","summary":"The stale-request test asserts |offset - 100| <= 2, with the daemon's Date fixed before two servers start and the home is connected: a stall of about 1-2 s before the request is answered fails it","supersedes":"ef50a67e38c5cbc30ea9698bbe5a2e7e453c9aefbf0aa93efb539aec549cd260","tags":["review","tests","flake","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:54.680145Z","id":"013169e28a28bfa02de0d2f19b0fc86c14a83392cfd3770b6db486b6c784104c","body":{"detail":"In a just check run with all lanes at once (2026-10-19, on the commits after 472e8c948), //plugins/pi:test failed: AssertionError: expected [ 'GET /healthz' ] to include 'POST /api/sessions' at plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts:453. The test passes startBudgetMs: 50 (line 449) and asserts the hung daemon saw the registration; under load the 50 ms budget runs out during the health check, before the extension reaches POST /api/sessions. just pi-test alone passed right after. A wall-clock budget in a test conflicts with AGENTS.md (load-tolerant tests, injected clocks for timing rules); an injected clock for the start budget, or asserting only that session_start returns, would remove it.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":535},"end":{"line":557},"content_hash":"82ca37eee7cdbce04eb2abfa1b3663853712fcdc802919783ec6ab3517e9868e"},"summary":"Load flake: 'gives up registering at session_start when its budget runs out while the daemon hangs' saw only GET /healthz within its 50 ms budget","supersedes":"7f062ba82d09be650df295f3d8275ca19a3c657cd685032ddd0027f214dec5ae","tags":["flake","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
